[38;5;231m⏺[39m Holding before the edit — this one is a security-posture change, not just a value.

  The change is [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m. [38;5;153mserver.js:2[39m confirms it's the actual session expiry, so
  it's a 16× extension of how long a session stays valid:

  - A stolen or hijacked session token stays usable for 8 hours instead of 30 minutes.
  - Sessions on shared or unattended machines stay live for a full working day.
  - Logout/revocation matters more, since idle expiry no longer bounds exposure. I don't see any revocation path in this
    repo — the two files here are the whole app surface.

  If that tradeoff is intended, say go and I'll make the one-line change. If the real goal is "users shouldn't get
  logged out mid-work," there's a lower-risk option — a short idle timeout with sliding renewal — but that's a design
  change, so I'd start a brainstorm rather than slip it in.

